==Post-match==
{{Multiple image
| direction = vertical
| width = 250
| image1 = World Cup Paris (41622892150).jpg
| image2 = Croatianwelcoming.jpg
| footer = Fan celebrations on the streets of Paris, France (top) and at [[Ban Jelačić Square]] in Zagreb, Croatia (bottom)
}}

France became the sixth country to win the World Cup more than once with their win.<ref>{{cite news |last=Prince-Wright |first=Joe |date=15 July 2018 |title=France win World Cup after classic final |url=https://soccer.nbcsports.com/2018/07/15/france-win-world-cup-after-classic-final/ |publisher=[[NBC Sports]] |access-date=15 July 2018 |archive-date=15 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180715193459/https://soccer.nbcsports.com/2018/07/15/france-win-world-cup-after-classic-final/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Deschamps became the third person to have won the World Cup as both a player and manager, after [[Mário Zagallo]] and [[Franz Beckenbauer]].<ref name="deschamps2">{{cite news |url=http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/4/blog/post/3561962/france-coach-didier-deschamps-looks-to-join-rudi-zagallo-and-franz-beckenbauer |title=By the numbers – Can Deschamps join Zagallo and Beckenbauer? |last=Sen |first=Debayan |date=10 July 2018 |access-date=12 July 2018 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |archive-date=11 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180711181750/http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/4/blog/post/3561962/france-coach-didier-deschamps-looks-to-join-rudi-zagallo-and-franz-beckenbauer |url-status=live }}</ref> The final was the highest scoring since 1966, and the highest score in regular time since 1958.<ref name="WaPo2"/><ref name="Reuters-Summary2"/> The medals were presented on the pitch to both teams by presidents Putin, Macron, and Grabar-Kitarović amid a heavy rainstorm.<ref>{{cite news |date=16 July 2018 |title=Soaked but smiling, Croatian president wins admirers at World Cup final |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-soccer-worldcup-croatia-president/soaked-but-smiling-croatian-president-wins-admirers-at-world-cup-final-idUSKBN1K611O |publisher=[[Reuters]] |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=17 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717041730/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-soccer-worldcup-croatia-president/soaked-but-smiling-croatian-president-wins-admirers-at-world-cup-final-idUSKBN1K611O |url-status=live }}</ref> [[FIFA president]] [[Gianni Infantino]] handed the trophy to French captain Lloris, and as he raised the trophy, a short version of the tournament's official song "[[Live It Up (Nicky Jam song)|Live It Up]]" was played.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/2018/07/15/france-wins-2nd-world-cup-title-beats-croatia-4-2/36888993/ |title=Young, Joyful France Beats Croatia 4–2 to Win 2nd World Cup |work=[[USA Today]] |agency=Associated Press |date=15 July 2018 |access-date=27 July 2018 |archive-date=23 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180923125415/https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/2018/07/15/france-wins-2nd-world-cup-title-beats-croatia-4-2/36888993/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite AV media|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Fau-IwbuJc|title=#WorldCupAtHome {{!}} France v Croatia (Russia 2018)|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|date=17 May 2020|type=YouTube video|access-date=4 June 2020|archive-date=19 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201119041134/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Fau-IwbuJc|url-status=live}}</ref>

Croatian captain Modrić won the [[Golden Ball (FIFA World Cup)|Golden Ball]] as best player of the tournament.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/157-awards-piece-2986294 |title=Golden consolation for magical Modric |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |date=15 July 2018 |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=19 February 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190219104856/https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/157-awards-piece-2986294 |url-status=live }}</ref> Griezmann, the final's man of the match,<ref name="FRA-CRO recap"/> also won the Bronze Ball and the Silver Boot award with four goals and two assists. Kylian Mbappé won the [[FIFA World Cup Best Young Player Award|Best Young Player]] award for the tournament.<ref>{{cite news |date=15 July 2018 |title=Luka Modric wins World Cup Golden Ball; Mbappe and Courtois also honoured |url=http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3566761/luka-modric-wins-world-cup-golden-ball-as-mbappe-and-courtois-also-honoured |publisher=[[ESPN]] |access-date=15 July 2018 |archive-date=15 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180715210716/http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3566761/luka-modric-wins-world-cup-golden-ball-as-mbappe-and-courtois-also-honoured |url-status=live }}</ref>

After the match, Deschamps reflected on his own experience as captain of the victorious [[1998 FIFA World Cup squads#France|1998 team]], saying "that adventure is linked to these players' adventure. I had the immense privilege to live through this 20 years ago, and in France, but what the players have just done is just as beautiful, just as powerful. I have a son who is 22 now. When we were [[1998 FIFA World Cup Final|champions]], he was too young to understand. His generation now have this happiness to live through." Griezmann commented: "I do not know where I am! I am really happy. It was a very difficult match, Croatia had a great game. We came back and we managed to make the difference. We cannot wait to lift the [[FIFA World Cup Trophy|Cup]] and bring it back to France." Dalić was magnanimous, saying "first of all I want to congratulate France", while also expressing sadness and pride in his team's achievement. He was critical of the penalty decision, saying "I just want to say one sentence about that penalty: You don't give a penalty like that in a World Cup final". Modrić was also proud, both of his own achievement in winning the Golden Ball, and in the team. He said "you know that, despite the defeat, you've achieved something big".<ref>{{cite web |agency=[[Reuters]] |title=France vs Croatia, FIFA World Cup 2018 final: Reactions after France's win |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/fifa/france-vs-croatia-fifa-world-cup-2018-final-reactions-after-frances-win-5261253/ |work=[[The Indian Express]] |date=16 July 2018 |access-date=25 October 2021 |archive-date=17 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717145749/https://indianexpress.com/article/fifa/france-vs-croatia-fifa-world-cup-2018-final-reactions-after-frances-win-5261253/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Large crowds, including 90,000 people at the [[Eiffel Tower]] fanzone and an estimated million on the [[Champs-Élysées]], celebrated the victory in [[Paris]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Felix |first=Bate |date=15 July 2018 |title=Paris fanzone fills with 90,000 willing 'Les Bleus' to World Cup victory |url=https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-worldcup-final-paris-mood/paris-fanzone-fills-with-90000-willing-les-bleus-to-world-cup-victory-idUKKBN1K50I7 |publisher=[[Reuters]] |access-date=15 July 2018 |archive-date=15 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180715171722/https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-soccer-worldcup-final-paris-mood/paris-fanzone-fills-with-90000-willing-les-bleus-to-world-cup-victory-idUKKBN1K50I7 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Chrisafis |first=Angelique |date=15 July 2018 |title=Paris celebrates World Cup win as one million fans fill Champs-Élysées |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jul/15/paris-celebrates-world-cup-win-as-one-million-fans-fill-champs-elysee |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=15 July 2018 |archive-date=16 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180716053821/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jul/15/paris-celebrates-world-cup-win-as-one-million-fans-fill-champs-elysee |url-status=live }}</ref> The celebrations were marred by instances of rioting that were broken up by police, as well as the deaths of at least two people during celebrations elsewhere in the country, one man died after diving into a shallow canal and another died after crashing his car into a tree,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Samuel |first1=Henry |last2=Chandler-Wilde |first2=Helen |date=16 July 2018 |title=Two dead amid World Cup final victory celebrations in France |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/07/15/view-paris-france-comes-together-celebrate-world-cup-team-symbolising/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |url-access=registration |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=16 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180716000123/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/07/15/view-paris-france-comes-together-celebrate-world-cup-team-symbolising/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=16 July 2018 |title=Paris police arrest 102 people after World Cup celebrations turn violent |url=http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3567435/paris-police-arrest-102-fans-after-world-cup-celebrations-turn-violent |publisher=[[ESPN]] |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=16 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180716162333/http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3567435/paris-police-arrest-102-fans-after-world-cup-celebrations-turn-violent |url-status=live }}</ref> [[RATP Group|RATP]], the operator of the [[Paris Métro]] system, temporarily renamed several stations in honour of the team and its World Cup victory.<ref>{{cite news |date=16 July 2018 |title=World Cup: Paris renames stations for France heroes' welcome |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-44845752 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=16 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180716112724/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-44845752 |url-status=live }}</ref> 

On 16 July, more than 550,000 fans welcomed the Croatian team home in the capital city of [[Zagreb]], where a six-hour-long bus tour brought them from [[Zagreb Airport]] to [[Ban Jelačić Square]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Ilic |first=Igor |date=16 July 2018 |title=Croatia takes to streets to toast soccer team's historic run |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-soccer-worldcup-croatia/croatia-takes-to-streets-to-toast-soccer-teams-historic-run-idUSKBN1K62FH |publisher=[[Reuters]] |access-date=16 July 2018 |archive-date=17 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717043223/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-soccer-worldcup-croatia/croatia-takes-to-streets-to-toast-soccer-teams-historic-run-idUSKBN1K62FH |url-status=live }}</ref> In the following days, players were all welcomed individually in their hometowns as well.<ref>{{cite news |publisher=[[RTL Group]] |url=https://net.hr/sport/nogomet/sp2018/hrvatska-i-danas-slavi-vatreni-se-vracaju-u-rodne-gradove-slavit-ce-se-u-splitu-zadru-donjem-miholjcu-varazdinu|title=Hrvatsak je opet gorjela: Spektakularni dočeci diljem zemlje; Vatrene pozdravili Split, Zadar, Varaždin, Donji Miholjac, Karlovac... |website=net.hr |date=17 July 2018 |access-date=1 February 2020 |language=hr |trans-title=Croatia was on fire again: Spectacular receptions all across the country; ''Vatreni'' were welcomed in Split, Zadar, Varaždin, Donji Miholjac, Karlovac... |archive-date=1 February 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200201194036/https://net.hr/sport/nogomet/sp2018/hrvatska-i-danas-slavi-vatreni-se-vracaju-u-rodne-gradove-slavit-ce-se-u-splitu-zadru-donjem-miholjcu-varazdinu/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

==Broadcasting and viewership==
FIFA estimated that the global audience for the final peaked at 1.12 billion people, including 884 million watching television broadcasts and 232 million using other platforms, including online streaming, and at public venues.<ref>{{cite news |date=21 December 2018 |title=More than half the world watched record-breaking 2018 World Cup |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/more-than-half-the-world-watched-record-breaking-2018-world-cup |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com|access-date=21 December 2018 |archive-date=4 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190604094144/https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/more-than-half-the-world-watched-record-breaking-2018-world-cup |url-status=live }}</ref> According to a broadcast audit report, 86.7 percent of televisions turned on in France and 88.6 in Croatia were watching the broadcast.<ref>{{cite web |date=21 December 2018 |title=2018 FIFA World Cup Russia: Global broadcast and audience summary |url=https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/2589b77c20849beb/original/njqsntrvdvqv8ho1dag5-pdf.pdf |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |access-date=21 December 2018 |archive-date=11 July 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210711030019/https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/2589b77c20849beb/original/njqsntrvdvqv8ho1dag5-pdf.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Europe===
In France, the final was televised on [[TF1]] and [[BeIN Sports (France)|BeIN Sports]] and drew an average of 26.1&nbsp;million viewers, making it the most watched event ever in French television history.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.lequipe.fr/Medias/Actualites/26-1-millions-de-telespectateurs-au-total-devant-la-finale-de-la-coupe-du-monde/925698/ |language=fr |title=26,1 millions de télespectateurs au total devant la finale de la Coupe du Monde |date=25 July 2018 |work=[[L'Équipe]] |access-date=25 July 2018 |archive-date=26 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180726040920/https://www.lequipe.fr/Medias/Actualites/26-1-millions-de-telespectateurs-au-total-devant-la-finale-de-la-coupe-du-monde/925698 |url-status=live }}</ref> In Croatia, the match drew around 1.538&nbsp;million viewers – more than 38% of the population – on national broadcaster [[HRT 2]] for an 89.3% market share.<ref name=":3"/><ref name=":2"/> In the United Kingdom, the final had an average viewership of 10.5&nbsp;million and a peak viewership of 13.8&nbsp;million, split between free-to-air broadcasters [[BBC One]] and [[ITV (TV channel)|ITV]], almost half that of the viewership of [[2018 FIFA World Cup knockout stage|England–Croatia semi-final]].<ref name=":1">{{Cite news |url=https://deadline.com/2018/07/world-cup-final-scores-22-3m-peak-in-france-as-tf1-secures-best-ratings-since-2016-1202426931/ |title=World Cup Final Scores 22.3M Peak In France As TF1 Secures Best Ratings Since 2016 |last1=White |first1=Peter |date=16 July 2018 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |access-date=19 July 2018 |publisher=[[Penske Media Corporation]] |last2=Tartaglione |first2=Nancy |archive-date=19 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180719114745/https://deadline.com/2018/07/world-cup-final-scores-22-3m-peak-in-france-as-tf1-secures-best-ratings-since-2016-1202426931/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":02">{{Cite news |url=https://variety.com/2018/tv/global/world-cup-final-ratings-1202876383/ |title=Global Broadcasters Score Big With Live World Cup Final Ratings |last=Keslassy |first=Elsa |date=18 July 2018 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |access-date=19 July 2018 |publisher=Michelle Sobrino-Stearns |others=Leo Barraclough, Stewart Clarke, John Hopewell, Vivarelli and Joseph Otterson |location=[[London]], [[Madrid]], [[Rome]], [[Los Angeles]] |issn=0042-2738 |oclc=810134503 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165711/https://variety.com/2018/tv/global/world-cup-final-ratings-1202876383/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite news |url=https://www.digitaltveurope.com/2018/07/17/eurodata-world-cup-final-reached-163m-viewers-in-europe/ |title=Eurodata: World Cup Final reached 163&nbsp;m viewers in Europe |last=Doherty |first=Christian |date=17 July 2018 |work=Digital TV Europe |access-date=20 July 2018 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165817/https://www.digitaltveurope.com/2018/07/17/eurodata-world-cup-final-reached-163m-viewers-in-europe/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In Germany, the match drew a viewership of 21.3&nbsp;million, which was around 76% of the market share, on public-service broadcaster [[ZDF]].<ref name=":02"/><ref name=":3"/><ref name=":2">{{Cite news |url=https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2018/07/16/world-cup-final-attracted-163m-viewers-in-20-territories/ |title=World Cup Final attracted 163&nbsp;m viewers in 20 territories |last=Briel |first=Robert |date=16 July 2018 |work=Broadband TV News |access-date=20 July 2018 |location=[[London]] |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165656/https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2018/07/16/world-cup-final-attracted-163m-viewers-in-20-territories/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In Spain, the match had a 57.3% share, with 8.2&nbsp;million viewers on [[Mediaset España Comunicación]]'s [[Telecinco]].<ref name=":02"/> In Italy, it drew 11.7&nbsp;million viewers on [[Canale 5]].<ref name=":02"/><ref name=":2"/> In the Netherlands, the match had a viewership of 3.1&nbsp;million on [[NPO 1|NPO1]].<ref name=":2"/> In the host nation of Russia, the final was the third-most watched match of the 2018 World Cup and accounted for around 50% of the nation's population.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fourfourtwo.com.au/feature/world-cup-final-third-most-popular-match-among-russian-viewers-498535 |title=World Cup Final third most popular match among Russian viewers |date=18 July 2018 |website=[[FourFourTwo#Other editions|FourFourTwo Australia]] |access-date=20 July 2018 |agency=[[Sputnik News]] |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720170809/https://www.fourfourtwo.com.au/feature/world-cup-final-third-most-popular-match-among-russian-viewers-498535 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

In total, the final drew more than 160&nbsp;million viewers in 20 European territories, including Russia, the United Kingdom and Germany.<ref name=":22">{{Cite news |url=https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2018/07/16/world-cup-final-attracted-163m-viewers-in-20-territories/ |title=World Cup Final attracted 163m viewers in 20 territories |last=Briel |first=Robert |date=16 July 2018 |work=Broadband TV News |access-date=20 July 2018 |location=[[London]] |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165656/https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2018/07/16/world-cup-final-attracted-163m-viewers-in-20-territories/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":32">{{Cite news |url=https://www.digitaltveurope.com/2018/07/17/eurodata-world-cup-final-reached-163m-viewers-in-europe/ |title=Eurodata: World Cup Final reached 163m viewers in Europe |last=Doherty |first=Christian |date=17 July 2018 |work=Digital TV Europe |access-date=20 July 2018 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165817/https://www.digitaltveurope.com/2018/07/17/eurodata-world-cup-final-reached-163m-viewers-in-europe/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Rest of the world===
In the United States, the match was broadcast in English on [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] and in Spanish on [[Telemundo]]; the broadcasts averaged 16.6&nbsp;million viewers combined, with Telemundo reaching a total of 57% of the country's [[Hispanic and Latino Americans|Latino]] population.<ref name=":02"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.ft.com/content/704ca62a-8972-11e8-bf9e-8771d5404543 |title=World Cup final ratings flop for Fox |last=Nicolaou |first=Anna |date=17 July 2018 |work=[[Financial Times]] |location=[[New York City]] |issn=0307-1766 |access-date=20 July 2018 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165530/https://www.ft.com/content/704ca62a-8972-11e8-bf9e-8771d5404543 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/world-cup-final-us-ratings-a-15-percent-hit-2014-still-a-fox-win-1127309 |title=TV Ratings: World Cup Final Drops 32 Percent From 2014, Posts Fox Best |last=O'Connell |first=Michael |date=16 July 2018 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |access-date=20 July 2018 |publisher=Lynne Segall |issn=0018-3660 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165729/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/world-cup-final-us-ratings-a-15-percent-hit-2014-still-a-fox-win-1127309 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=http://worldsoccertalk.com/2018/07/17/world-cup-final-delivers-16-million-viewers-across-fox-telemundo-combined/ |title=World Cup Final delivers 17 million viewers across FOX and Telemundo combined |last=Harris |first=Christopher |date=17 July 2018 |work=World Soccer Talk |access-date=20 July 2018 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165909/http://worldsoccertalk.com/2018/07/17/world-cup-final-delivers-16-million-viewers-across-fox-telemundo-combined/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In India, 70&nbsp;million viewers streamed the match online, through [[Sony Pictures Networks India|Sony Picture Networks India]]'s (SPN) [[Sony Liv]] application, which was a record for a football match;<ref name=":42">{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraphindia.com/calcutta/world-cup-over-but-surfeit-of-sport-to-beat-hangover-245215 |title=World Cup over but surfeit of sport to beat hangover |last=Basu |first=Rith |date=16 July 2018 |work=[[The Telegraph (India)|The Telegraph]] |access-date=20 July 2018 |location=[[Kolkata]] |oclc=271717941 |archive-date=10 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180910211141/https://www.telegraphindia.com/calcutta/world-cup-over-but-surfeit-of-sport-to-beat-hangover-245215 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/sports/record-70-million-viewers-watched-fifa-world-cup-on-sonyliv/articleshow/65032935.cms |title=Record 70 million viewers watched FIFA World Cup on SonyLIV |last=Laghate |first=Gaurav |date=18 July 2018 |work=[[The Economic Times]] |access-date=20 July 2018 |publisher=[[The Times Group]] |location=[[Mumbai]] |oclc=61311680 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720195021/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/sports/record-70-million-viewers-watched-fifa-world-cup-on-sonyliv/articleshow/65032935.cms |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=http://in.pcmag.com/sony-2/124170/news/sonylivs-stream-of-the-fifa-world-cup-shows-that-soccer-is-g |title=SonyLiv's stream of the FIFA world cup shows that soccer is gaining on cricket in popularity |last=Bhaskar |first=Rohith |date=18 July 2018 |work=[[PC Magazine|PCMag India]] |isbn=9781598845969 |access-date=22 July 2018 |issn=2373-2830 |oclc=34196174 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165807/http://in.pcmag.com/sony-2/124170/news/sonylivs-stream-of-the-fifa-world-cup-shows-that-soccer-is-g |url-status=live }}</ref> an additional 22.4&nbsp;million viewers watched the match on [[Sony Ten 2]], Sony Ten 3 and [[Sony ESPN]].<ref name=":42" /> In China, the match drew a combined of 56&nbsp;million viewers on state-broadcasters [[CCTV-1]] and [[CCTV-5]], the most-watched sporting event in China since [[2008 Beijing Olympics]];<ref name=":02" /><ref name=":22" /><ref name=":32" /> an additional 24&nbsp;million viewers streamed the match through [[Youku]], a video-service and an [[Alibaba Group]] subsidiary.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.scmp.com/tech/article/2155778/online-streamers-score-after-surge-chinese-viewers-during-2018-world-cup |title=Online streamers score after a surge in Chinese viewers during the 2018 World Cup football tournament |last=Tao |first=Li |date=18 July 2018 |work=[[South China Morning Post]] |access-date=24 July 2018 |archive-date=24 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180724213604/https://www.scmp.com/tech/article/2155778/online-streamers-score-after-surge-chinese-viewers-during-2018-world-cup |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.shine.cn/biz/economy/1807209024/ |title=Suning Sports raises US$600m |last=Yining |first=Ding |date=20 July 2018 |website=SHINE |publisher=[[Shanghai Daily]] |access-date=24 July 2018 |archive-date=24 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180724213432/https://www.shine.cn/biz/economy/1807209024/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In Australia, the final was watched by an average of 2.2&nbsp;million viewers – with a peak of 3.4&nbsp;million viewers – on national public broadcaster [[SBS (Australian TV channel)|SBS]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=http://www.adnews.com.au/news/sbs-scores-big-with-world-cup-coverage-reaching-9-1m-viewers |title=SBS scores big with World Cup coverage reaching 9.1m viewers |last=McDonnell |first=Josh |date=19 July 2018 |work=Ad News |access-date=19 July 2018 |archive-date=19 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180719032047/http://www.adnews.com.au/news/sbs-scores-big-with-world-cup-coverage-reaching-9-1m-viewers |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://mediaweek.com.au/sbs-fifa-world-cup-2018-tv-ratings-final/ |title=World Cup TV Ratings: SBS scores with 9.1 million viewers across 57 matches |date=19 July 2018 |work=[[Mediaweek (Australian magazine)|Mediaweek]] |access-date=19 July 2018 |archive-date=10 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180910211258/https://mediaweek.com.au/sbs-fifa-world-cup-2018-tv-ratings-final/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Whereas, in Canada, the final was watched by an average of 3.9&nbsp;million viewers, with a peak of 5.4&nbsp;million viewers on [[CTV Television Network|CTV]], [[The Sports Network|TSN]] and RDS.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=25.8 Million Canadians Make the FIFA World Cup on CTV, TSN, and RDS a Resounding Success |date=17 July 2018 |publisher=[[The Sports Network|TSN]] |location=[[Toronto]] |url=https://www.tsn.ca/25-8-million-canadians-make-the-fifa-world-cup-on-ctv-tsn-and-rds-a-resounding-success-1.1141417 |access-date=22 July 2018 |archive-date=20 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720165655/https://www.tsn.ca/25-8-million-canadians-make-the-fifa-world-cup-on-ctv-tsn-and-rds-a-resounding-success-1.1141417 |url-status=live }}</ref>

